 ],
 "notes": "Photos 02, 03 and the lake views (sheet0 and sheet2): from the water the place stands in layers - a stone-edged shore with a long wood dock, a small dark boathouse with a pitched slate roof and big glass doors on the lawn, then the house climbing a sloping, treed bank. The house reads as three storeys on the lake side: a lighter (white render) walk-out level with sliding glass under a deck, a white middle level with full-width glazing opening to a furnished timber terrace with a black cable-rail and slender black posts, and a dark upper level with a glazed band and a balcony; low pitched slate roofs, a gable pointing at the lake on the west end. Arrival side (north) is more closed, dark upper walls over light ones, and there is a stair of wood down the east side of the lawn. Interiors (kitchen island, floating stair, laundry) were not modelled. Round 1 render showed the house as three equal slabs with a flat top; round 2 added the gable roofs and wing; round 3 swapped the upper gable (which buried the dark walls) for a thin low slate roof, widened the lawn to the shore, deepened the terrace glass recess and moved the boathouse and dock to the lawn edge. Guessed: footprint and every dimension (scaled by storey height 3 m), orientation (lake south), the extent of the dark upper level, the number of trees and their positions, the east stair (shown only as a walk). Placed at its town only; no site more exact than the region."
